WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:06.865
For sixteen values and eight threads per
block, each thread in block zero copies one

00:00:06.865 --> 00:00:08.202
value into scratch.

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:13.085
Scratch is shared memory that the threads
in the same block can access.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.263
Thread one stores two, while thread five
stores six.

00:00:17.443 --> 00:00:21.228
Each must reach the block barrier before
any thread continues.

00:00:21.408 --> 00:00:25.669
The barrier lets thread one read the value
written by thread five.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:32.656
At a distance of four, thread one reads
scratch at index five and adds six to its

00:00:32.656 --> 00:00:33.027
two.

00:00:33.207 --> 00:00:37.190
The notebook experiment prints those two
inputs from inside the kernel.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:44.454
In the nineteen value case, the last block
starts with three inputs and five zeros.

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:46.713
All eight threads reach the barrier.

00:00:46.893 --> 00:00:52.094
Compare the sum of those three inputs with
the last output printed by main.
